My current finding is that the cyclicity condition forces the incircle radius to satisfy \(r^{2}=BD\cdot CD=F_{n}F_{n+1}\), so \(r=\sqrt{F_{n}F_{n+1}}\). Substituting this into the geometry yields the exact closed‑form  
\[
\frac{CT\cdot NB}{BT\cdot NE}
=\frac12\sqrt{\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_{n}}+6+\frac{F_{n}}{F_{n+1}}}
\]  
and therefore the limit \(\alpha=\frac12\sqrt{6+\sqrt5}\). This shows that the earlier claim \(\alpha=(3+\sqrt5)/2\) (or any representation \(\alpha=p+\sqrt q\) with rational \(p,q\)) is incorrect.
